WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.077
What if an indicator could open a whole new perspective? Step

00:00:03.077 --> 00:00:06.154
through the digital looking glass. Meet Pivotglass: a

00:00:06.154 --> 00:00:09.231
workspace for asking better questions, following evidence, and seeing

00:00:09.231 --> 00:00:12.308
an investigation take shape. Start with a question, an indicator, or a

00:00:12.308 --> 00:00:15.385
report. Guided coaching helps new analysts get moving.

00:00:15.385 --> 00:00:18.462
Preview local documents, choose what to admit, and open complete

00:00:18.462 --> 00:00:21.538
source details. Every step gives you something you can

00:00:21.538 --> 00:00:24.615
inspect. Then change your perspective. Follow typed

00:00:24.615 --> 00:00:27.692
relationships. Reconstruct provenance and analyst groups.

00:00:27.692 --> 00:00:30.769
Scan the constellation for uneven coverage. A crowded

00:00:30.769 --> 00:00:33.846
case becomes a set of questions you can actually work. Twelve evidence

00:00:33.846 --> 00:00:36.923
views reveal different sides of the same workspace: stored

00:00:36.923 --> 00:00:40.000
types, Dossier completeness, investigation and enrichment

00:00:40.000 --> 00:00:43.077
activity, connection counts, and coverage similarity. The view

00:00:43.077 --> 00:00:46.154
explains its question and exposes its exact data. Compare

00:00:46.154 --> 00:00:49.231
competing hypotheses. Explore the investigation

00:00:49.231 --> 00:00:52.308
hierarchy. Keep likelihood separate from confidence.

00:00:52.308 --> 00:00:55.385
Structured techniques make assumptions, contradictions, and next
collection

00:00:55.385 --> 00:00:58.462
needs visible. Then turn the work into a reviewable

00:00:58.462 --> 00:01:01.538
report, saved as Markdown or printed to PDF. Choose your

00:01:01.538 --> 00:01:04.615
atmosphere, including original generative music. Begin

00:01:04.615 --> 00:01:07.692
locally with the synthetic quickstart, then enable services

00:01:07.692 --> 00:01:10.769
deliberately. Download Pivotglass from github dot com slash

00:01:10.769 --> 00:01:13.846
jarocki slash pivotglass. Follow a connection. Ask a

00:01:13.846 --> 00:01:16.615
sharper question. Discover what the evidence can show.
